The latest inspected implementation retains a relay fallback/lifecycle regression. TypeScript checking passed; rail and scatter issues corrected during this review are excluded.

Review comment:

- [P2] Stop relay discovery when terrain cannot mount — /Users/robin/Claude/Projects/Gold Rush/worktrees/lane-b/src/systems/RelaySignalPresentation.ts:43-47
  On Relay Rush in LITE mode, with terrain disabled, or after a terrain load failure, the relay models never enter the scene (`Terrain3dClaimPilot.ts:3119–3122` explicitly skips them for LITE). `complete` therefore stays false and this loop recursively searches the entire scene four times every frame indefinitely. An isolated probe with 1,000 children performed 4,004 object visits per frame. The zero-binding teardown also never restores `scene.onBeforeRender`: cleanup depends on a bound material being disposed, while Game discards the owner. Connect discovery and cleanup to terrain completion/failure/cancellation, including disposal before the first binding.
